.TH MARKSIGHT 1 "2026-10-07" "marksight 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
marksight \- minimal, theme-native markdown viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marksight
.RI [ FILE ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B marksight
renders a Markdown document with native GTK 4 widgets, following the desktop
theme automatically. It implements CommonMark plus GitHub-flavored tables,
task lists, footnotes, strikethrough and alerts. Raw HTML in documents is
dropped, never rendered.
.PP
The viewed file is watched for changes and re-rendered shortly after every
save. A table-of-contents sidebar and find-in-document are built in.
Each file given on the command line, including files opened while marksight
is already running, opens in a window of its own; opening a file that is
already on screen raises its existing window instead.
Links to web pages (http, https) and email addresses (mailto) open in the
system's configured application; every other link scheme is ignored.
In-document links jump to footnotes and to headings that carry an explicit
{#id} attribute.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a file
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Find in document
.TP
.B Enter / Shift+Enter
Next / previous match
.TP
.B F9
Toggle the contents sidebar
.TP
.B Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Q
Close window / quit
.SH FILES
Opened through the file portal, so marksight needs no direct filesystem
permissions when sandboxed.
